  "facts": [
    "Montague Street Tunnel, opened August 1, 1920, was engineered by Clifford Milburn Holland, later chief engineer of the Holland Tunnel, and cost nearly $10 million, double the 60th Street Tunnel's price.",
    "On December 27, 1920, a shoe beam caused a short circuit, trapping ten trains and forcing a mass evacuation of over ten thousand passengers from the tunnel.",
    "After Hurricane Sandy flooded the tunnel in October 2012, it closed for a full reconstruction, reopening a month early on September 15, 2014, after extensive repairs."
